Chapter: WorkflowParseIntTest
  cites Wflow chapter ProcessEngine (parse-int)

 ProcessEngine's parse-int read ASCII digit codes in a CCE world, so it
 returned 0 for every number it was given. Nothing caught it because the
 only callers are the GreaterThan and LessThan gate conditions, and a
 gate that compares 0 against its threshold still answers True or False.
 It just answers the same one every time.

 The value lines are the test. A gate line alone would not be, since
 both a working parse and a broken one produce a Boolean.

Section: Entry
  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni ("parse 42 = " & show (parse-int "42"))
   print-line-uni ("parse 0 = " & show (parse-int "0"))
   print-line-uni ("parse 1009 = " & show (parse-int "1009"))
   print-line-uni ("parse empty = " & show (parse-int ""))
   print-line-uni ("parse 7x = " & show (parse-int "7x"))
  end
